Description: imagesetinterpolation() and imagescale() with IMG_BICUBIC (GD_BICUBIC, GD_BICUBIC_FIXED) failed with libgd 2.3.3: its gdImageSetInterpolationMethod() lost their case (libgd issue #847); PHP gd of every version takes this libgd; and CVE-2026-9672, the LZW decoder of GIF (gd_gif_in.c, imagecreatefromgif() of PHP): the second row of its table left uninitialised (table[1][0] set in its place), the data after the end code read on, the decoder state uninitialised; and imagerotate() of a palette image (GIF, PNG8): by 180 degrees gdImageRotateInterpolated() destroyed the image of the caller instead of its truecolor copy and rotated it then (libgd #810: a use-after-free, and PHP frees that image again, a double free), by another angle with IMG_NEAREST_NEIGHBOUR it rotated the palette image, which has no truecolor pixels (libgd #929: a crash), and by 0 degrees it gave back a palette clone and leaked nothing only by chance (the truecolor copy is returned now, as upstream)
Origin: upstream https://github.com/libgd/libgd/commit/39abd7238cea2ba8baa4bcac1d6fc01c6cb8afab (in libgd master, no release yet), the hunk of src/gd_interpolation.c as Gentoo carries it (media-libs/gd files/gd-2.3.3-GD_BICUBIC.patch), -p0; CVE-2026-9672: the fix openSUSE carries (gd 2.3.3, gd-CVE-2026-9672.patch of 03.08.2026, bsc#1273101, https://github.com/bmwiedemann/openSUSE/blob/master/packages/g/gd/gd-CVE-2026-9672.patch), the code the libgd bundled in PHP has had since 5.6 (libgd master still lacks it); #810 and #929: upstream https://github.com/libgd/libgd/commit/6cc1e39e9fddd15ae74adb1a09fcd5740f44923e (29.01.2022) and https://github.com/libgd/libgd/commit/a656f5cc5592757996e9e96b0821a0966bfaa3b3 (09.01.2025), in libgd master, no release yet, as Debian carries them on 2.3.3 (libgd2 2.3.3-16, debian/patches/0007-Fix-810-Wrong-image-freed-src_cloned-should-be-freed.patch and 0008-Fix-fix-for-320-929.patch), -p0

--- src/gd_interpolation.c
+++ src/gd_interpolation.c
@@ -2257,6 +2257,11 @@ BGD_DECLARE(int) gdImageSetInterpolationMethod(gdImagePtr im, gdInterpolationMet
 		case GD_BESSEL:
 			im->interpolation = filter_bessel;
 			break;
+		case GD_BICUBIC_FIXED:
+		case GD_BICUBIC:
+			/* no interpolation as gdImageScale calls a dedicated function */
+			im->interpolation = NULL;
+			break;
 		case GD_BLACKMAN:
 			im->interpolation = filter_blackman;
 			break;
--- src/gd_gif_in.c
+++ src/gd_gif_in.c
@@ -530,7 +530,7 @@ LWZReadByte_(gdIOCtx *fd, LZW_STATIC_DAT
 		}
 
 		for(; i < (1 << MAX_LWZ_BITS); ++i) {
-			sd->table[0][i] = sd->table[1][0] = 0;
+			sd->table[0][i] = sd->table[1][i] = 0;
 		}
 
 		sd->sp = sd->stack;
@@ -584,6 +584,8 @@ LWZReadByte_(gdIOCtx *fd, LZW_STATIC_DAT
 			if(count != 0) {
 				return -2;
 			}
+
+			return -2;
 		}
 
 		incode = code;
@@ -664,7 +666,7 @@ ReadImage(gdImagePtr im, gdIOCtx *fd, in
 	unsigned char c;
 	int xpos = 0, ypos = 0, pass = 0;
 	int v, i;
-	LZW_STATIC_DATA sd;
+	LZW_STATIC_DATA sd = {0};
 
 	/* Initialize the Compression routines */
 	if(!ReadOK(fd, &c, 1)) {
